courses/
.verify-export.*
__pycache__/

# A generated recipe mirror the launchers create inside a working folder
# (the repo root becomes one when the launchers are run in place).
.toolchain/

# Windows app build output
windows-app/**/bin/
windows-app/**/obj/
website/shots/windowshot/bin/
website/shots/windowshot/obj/

# Repo-local Claude skills are shared content the whole team (and the
# Windows machine) needs — un-ignore them past the global rule that
# hides .claude/ everywhere. Anything else in .claude/ stays private.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# ...except the teachers' printing skill, which the app writes into any
# working folder it opens - and this repository is one (it has preview.sh at
# its root). Its source is support/agent_guidance; a copy here would load the
# teachers' skill into this repository's own sessions (#454 review N5).
.claude/skills/plantoir-printing/
/.agents/

# Release bundles (publish output)
windows-app/dist/
mac-app/dist/
mac-app/build/

# llama.cpp builds, fetched by Vendor/fetch-llama scripts.
# ~25-35 MB of build output; the scripts pin the version.
mac-app/Vendor/llama
# Sparkle (the app finding and installing its own updates, #204), fetched by
# mac-app/Vendor/fetch-sparkle.sh — pinned by version and SHA-256, never committed.
mac-app/Vendor/Sparkle
# A dress-rehearsal feed (#204) is deployed by hand and deleted after; never committed.
website/updates/rehearsal-*/
windows-app/Vendor/llama/

# The native Windows toolchain runtime (node, python, patched Quartz,
# wrangler), fetched by Vendor/fetch-runtime.ps1 — ~600 MB of pinned output.
windows-app/Vendor/runtime/

# What `dotnet test --blame` / `--blame-crash` writes when diagnosing a test
# host that died: a small TestResults/<guid>/<guid>_Sequence.xml naming the
# test that was running,
# and - for --blame-crash - a FULL process dump, which is tens to hundreds of
# megabytes. Added 2026-09-08 alongside windows-app/TestRunOutcome.ps1, which
# tells people to reach for --blame; recommending a flag that stages a dump
# would be a poor trade.
TestResults/
*.dmp

# The website builder's helper programs and starting disk (~470 MB), fetched by
# mac-app/Vendor/fetch-helpers.sh (GitHub #312), and its staging folders.
mac-app/Vendor/helpers/
mac-app/Vendor/helpers
mac-app/Vendor/.helpers.*/

# Update-signing keys never live in the repository (#337): the private key stays
# in %USERPROFILE%\.plantoir-release, outside every clone.
*.priv
netsparkle*.key


# site/updates/ is a build-time copy of website/updates/ (build.py); the deploy reads the working copy, and git would normalise the Windows feed's CR LF
site/updates/
